							<p align="center"><font color="#deb887" size="6"><strong>Welcome to&nbsp;Storm Rider Rebellion<br /></strong></font></p> <p align="center"><font color="#f5f5dc" size="5"><strong></strong></font>&nbsp;</p> <p align="left"><font color="#f5f5dc" size="5"><strong>OUR&nbsp; MISSION<img src="/pics/2112/stormrider.JPG" align="right" /></strong></font></p> <p align="left"><font color="#d3d3d3">&nbsp;</font><font color="#d3d3d3"> <font size="4">We are a family-style raid guild.&nbsp; We are&nbsp;presently&nbsp;finishing up&nbsp;with Tier One of PoP progression and working on Tier Two targets.&nbsp;&nbsp;Our goals are to have fun, to share the great friendship that our guild provides,&nbsp;and to reach the elemental planes and Time.&nbsp;&nbsp;We are also working the OoW zones as well as DoN progression.&nbsp; </font></font></p> <p align="left"><font color="#d3d3d3"><font size="4">Storm Rider Rebellion&nbsp;is a thriving, active guild, and as such, we need people who are ready to contribute and participate in all of our endeavors.&nbsp; We will require a little more of you than some&nbsp;purely family-style&nbsp;guilds will.&nbsp; We are looking for people who like to raid, if you don't like raiding, then&nbsp;SRR might not be the right guild for you.</font></font></p> <p align="left"><font color="#d3d3d3" size="4">Our mission is to provide assistance to our brothers and sisters-in-arms and to help them advance and achieve their goals.&nbsp; We are people of honor and have high expectations for our guild members with regard to their conduct.&nbsp; We have no tolerance for those who disregard the rights of others.</font></p> <p align="center"><font color="#f5f5dc" size="5"><strong>OUR CODE OF CONDUCT</strong></font></p> <p align="left"><font size="4"><font color="#d3d3d3">Keep in mind that whatever you do or say reflects on all of us as&nbsp;a whole.&nbsp;&nbsp;Carry yourself&nbsp;with honor and dignity and bring credit upon&nbsp;SRR.&nbsp; <br /></font></p></font> <p align="left"><font color="#d3d3d3" size="4">Remember, that not all of our members are adults.&nbsp; We have young people in our midst and we should be mindful of that when making crude and sexually suggestive comments.&nbsp; Not everyone finds such banter entertaining.&nbsp; Keep guild chat respectful.</font></p> <p align="left"><font color="#d3d3d3" size="4">Go guild first.&nbsp; If you are forming an XP&nbsp;or LDoN group, ask guildies if they&nbsp;are available before recruiting outside the guild.&nbsp; Get to know the other people in your guild and incorporate them into your adventures.&nbsp; The more you group together, the more familiar you become with each others styles and the better we all raid together.</font></p> <p align="left"><font color="#d3d3d3" size="4">Be a recruiter for your guild.&nbsp; Keep your eyes open for unguilded players who exhibit good skills and &nbsp;good attitudes.&nbsp; We need such people.&nbsp; If you notice a good candidate for our guild, please contact any officer to arrange an invitation.</font></p> <p align="left"><font color="#d3d3d3" size="4">No begging, period.&nbsp; Do not expect your guild to outfit you with gear, to buff you&nbsp;or&nbsp;to level you.&nbsp;&nbsp; Everyone in&nbsp;Storm Rider Rebellion &nbsp;has a limited amount of time online.&nbsp; Each of us has goals we want to reach.&nbsp; Do not expect your guildies to sacrifice their time in order maximize yours.&nbsp; Now, with that said, most of us give freely of our time and resources to PL guildies and to give them needed gear and assistance.&nbsp; We love to do this and will gladly do it to help our guildies advance.&nbsp; But, the point is to let the person ask you if you'd like to be PL'd...... don't bug other people to PL you or to give you gear or buffs.</font></p> <p align="left"><font color="#d3d3d3" size="4">Do not ever recruit using /shout or /ooc.&nbsp; Our guild is selective in whom we accept and we do not recruit in open channels.&nbsp; If you have a candidate for membership in&nbsp;Storm Rider Rebellion, please give them our website address or contact an officer for assistance.</font></p> <p align="left"><font color="#d3d3d3" size="4">Do the right thing.&nbsp; If you get the chance to help someone, whether they are a guildie or not, do it.&nbsp; Give some free buffs,&nbsp; rez someone who is in need without charge,&nbsp; heal a lowbie who is in over their head in a fight.&nbsp; You are wearing the&nbsp;SRR guild tag and your kindness and generosity will be noticed and our guild will be strengthened by your good deeds.</font></p> <p align="left">&nbsp;</p>
							
